  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide life-preserving services to communities affected by the disaster.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">APDRF will be used for (i) provision of medical kits, food, and bottled drinking water; (ii) purchase of water purification and sanitation systems; (iii) provision of emergency and transitory shelter; and (iv) provision of personal hygiene kits. 
Progress/Status: Emergency assistance was provided for the permanent relocation of people from Ambae to other neighboring islands in Vanuatu.

ADB received the audit report from the government on 30 December 2019. The report was endorsed by ADB on 16 January 2020 and requested financial closing on 23 January 2020. 
Data Source: UN OCHA, VAN NDMO 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
